[gd_scene load_steps=7 format=3 uid="uid://unittextmeshhinting"]

; The one variable: a small `font_size` on a TextMesh with a TrueType font. Godot hints the outline at
; the size with the font's own bytecode, so the stems and the crossbar snap to whole pixels, and the
; `pixel_size` scales the snapped outline up. The left text is at 12 px and the right one at 17 px,
; and each `pixel_size` gives the same height as unit-text-mesh.tscn at 64 px. Both texts are flat.
; Every other TrueType TextMesh golden is at 64 px, where the hints move the outline less.

